    "question": "Marky owns a computer accessory shop. For this month, half of their sales are wireless mice, one-fourth are optical mice, and the rest are trackball mice. If Marky's shop was able to sell a total of 80 mice, how many of them are trackball mice?",
    "gold": "20",
    "answer": "There were 80/2 = <<80/2=40>>40 wireless mice sold.\nThere were 80/4 = <<80/4=20>>20 optical mice sold.\nSo, there were a total of 40 + 20 = <<40+20=60>>60 wireless and optical mice sold.\nTherefore, 80 - 60 = <<80-60=20>>20 trackball mice were sold this month.\n#### 20"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the number of trackball mice sold by Marky's shop, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of mice sold:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total mice sold} = 80\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the number of wireless mice sold:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Wireless mice} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 80 = 40\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of optical mice sold:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Optical mice} = \\frac{1}{4} \\times 80 = 20\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the number of trackball mice sold by subtracting the number of wireless and optical mice from the total:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Trackball mice} = 80 - (\\text{Wireless mice} + \\text{Optical mice})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Trackball mice} = 80 - (40 + 20) = 80 - 60 = 20\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of trackball mice sold is \\(\\boxed{20}\\).",
